   $q$Nadia "had played that note in rehearsal a thousand times." What is the role of this hyperbole in the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It suggests that the orchestra's rehearsals lasted far too long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It stresses how familiar the note is, making her nerves surprising.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It tells the reader the exact number of rehearsals she attended.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that she rarely practiced and felt unprepared that night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It stresses how familiar the note is, making her nerves surprising.$q$, $q$The exaggeration emphasizes that the note should feel routine, which sets up the contrast with "yet tonight her hands felt as if they belonged to a stranger." It is not a real count, so reading it as an exact number misses its purpose.$q$, 'draft', 'b5771e20-4539-5867-a8a1-125a9250a969')
