values
  ('d0526517-6c69-5da5-bf34-d6d82b4b1d72', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Priya says, "I hated every step of that hill," while grinning, and the coach replies, "Good. That means you finally respected it." What does this exchange show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Priya's complaint is playful, and the coach sees the struggle as proof she paced it wisely.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Priya is announcing that she plans to quit the team because of the hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The coach is glad Priya is unhappy because she thinks runners should suffer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The coach is being sarcastic because Priya still ran the hill the wrong way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Priya's complaint is playful, and the coach sees the struggle as proof she paced it wisely.$q$, $q$Priya's grin shows her "hated every step" is exaggeration after a good race, and the coach links feeling the hill's difficulty to finally treating it with the patience she advised. Priya followed the coach's method, so the coach is not being sarcastic.$q$, 'draft', '58f2c27b-5111-5491-9882-ceb303dad66f')
