   $q$Marisol tells Luis to count "every bulb that has ever wandered in here." What does "wandered in" suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Customers often carry bulbs around the store while shopping.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Marisol carefully orders every bulb the shop needs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Items arrive over time without anyone keeping careful track.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bulbs are kept in many different rooms on purpose.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Items arrive over time without anyone keeping careful track.$q$, $q$Describing bulbs as if they walked in on their own suggests they pile up unnoticed, which fits the later discovery of bulbs "nobody remembered buying." That discovery also rules out the idea that Marisol orders every bulb carefully.$q$, 'draft', 'ec8d744b-1d31-56d1-934a-eec6d0c0236b')
