values
  ('1e67e478-33ab-51ca-aa85-cb00bf942f19', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The author writes that "a warm afternoon on a loading dock can destroy centuries of evidence." What is the role of this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It explains that ice cores are usually stored on loading docks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"It shows that ice cores are too sturdy to be easily damaged.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It argues that loading docks should be kept closed in summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It contrasts a brief, small mistake with an enormous, lasting loss.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It contrasts a brief, small mistake with an enormous, lasting loss.$q$, $q$Setting "a warm afternoon" against "centuries of evidence" shows how fragile and irreplaceable the cores are, supporting the claim that the work is painstaking. The sentence stresses fragility, so it cannot show that cores are sturdy.$q$, 'draft', '749dcbcc-aaba-5b63-9630-c346625f1c23')
