  ('9b264076-8c8a-5746-8cec-b59ec1d09149', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$According to the passage, what does the metaphor "link rot" suggest about how links fail?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Links fail all at once when the whole internet shuts down suddenly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"Links fail slowly and quietly over time, often without anyone noticing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Links fail because computers become physically moldy and damaged.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Links are broken on purpose by people who dislike certain websites.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Links fail slowly and quietly over time, often without anyone noticing.$q$, $q$The author explains that "rot suggests something slow, quiet, and natural," like fruit spoiling unnoticed. The passage states that "no one decides to break them," so the idea of deliberate breaking contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '2c939315-9602-56db-a4ae-170c85dba003')
